<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal steady, oil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal steady, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in  central Indian markets in very thin trading. Business volume was dull  and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>More than 5.5 million hectares have been covered by soybean, an all-time  high that has met the target of 5.5 million hectares set by the Soybean  Processor's Association of India (SOPA), the apex body of the soybean  pressing industry.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were bearish on increased selling from plants and refineries.  Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down  by 200 rupees per tonne. Business volume was dull and the undertone  was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed prices were almost steady. Soymeal yellow was  $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west Indian ports for  export. Rapeseed extraction was $95-96 per tonne FAS (Free alongside  ship) in bulk for export and was 3,225-3,275 rupees per tonne in FOR  (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
